# Shipyard CLI

[Shipyard](https://goshipyard.app) is a feed for vibe-coded projects. Drive it with
the `shipyard` CLI (public API at `https://goshipyard.app/api/v1`, authed by the
user's personal API key). Add `--json` to any command for parseable output.

## First, confirm auth

```sh
shipyard whoami            # prints @handle — if so, you're ready
```

- `command not found` → install: `curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jonnonz1/goshipyard/main/install.sh | sh`
- "Not authenticated" → user creates a key at https://goshipyard.app/settings (API keys), then `shipyard login` (paste it). Never invent a key.

## Common tasks

```sh
# Post a project (title, pitch, url required)
shipyard projects create -t "Foglight" -p "Maps for makers" -u https://foglight.app -c devtools --hero ./shot.png

# List / inspect / edit your postings
shipyard projects list --mine
shipyard projects get <id>                 # upvotes + review counts
shipyard projects update <id> -p "Sharper pitch"
shipyard projects delete <id> -y

# Reviews (comments) — read & write (≥20 chars, honest, specific)
shipyard reviews list <id>
shipyard reviews add <id> -b "Tried it on a big graph — clustering held up, legend overlapped on mobile."
shipyard reviews mine

# Likes (upvotes) — idempotent
shipyard like <id>
shipyard unlike <id>

# Wallet — credit funds paid review bounties (fastest path to vetted reviews)
shipyard wallet
shipyard wallet topup --open               # load credit in the browser (Stripe)
```

## Rules

- Parse `--json`; don't scrape tables. Non-zero exit = failure.
- Preserve `review_source` when summarizing: `automated`, `seeded`, or `member`.
  Member is not verified hands-on testing. Missing provenance means unknown;
  payment alone does not establish a human source.
- Confirm public/irreversible actions (post, review, delete) with the user first.
- Never fabricate reviews/pitches/results — write from what was actually built.
- Don't bulk-like or spam low-content reviews to game rankings.
- Local dev: pass `--api-url http://localhost:3000`.
- Help: `shipyard help` or `shipyard <command> help`.
- No CLI? A hosted MCP server exposes overlapping capabilities at
  `https://goshipyard.app/mcp` (add `Authorization: Bearer sk_live_…`). Setup:
  https://github.com/jonnonz1/goshipyard/blob/main/docs/mcp.md
- CLI supports local uploads and project edits/deletion; MCP additionally supports
  `reply_to_review` and bounty funding. Follow `pagination.next_offset` when
  listing MCP projects, stopping when it is null.
